Context:

{noformat}When you set the address to Ulica grada Chicaga 25 and search for kfc, the KFC City Centar One East does not appear in results.
If you set the address to Ulica grada Chicaga it appears.{noformat}

I have put logs and I found the following issue for the KFC City Center One East (provider id 5164):

* When the user has delivery address as {{Ulica Grada Chicaga 25}},  the following are true (the most important part being the distance to eater *7.66 km*

{noformat}{
      "coordinates": {
        "lat": 45.80159,
        "lng": 16.05057
      },
      "distance": 7.66,
      "id": 5164
},
"user_location": {
    "lat": 45.786561,
    "lng": 16.006262
}{noformat}

* For the same address without number {{Ulica Grada Chicaga}}, we have:

{noformat}{
      "coordinates": {
        "lat": 45.80159,
        "lng": 16.05057
      },
      "distance": 4.87,
      "id": 5164
},
"user_location": {
    "lat": 45.788166,
    "lng": 16.00637
}{noformat}

Problem is that on {{delivery-provider-search}} we filter all providers that have a distance to eater < "custom_delivery_radius_in_km" for that provider (in this case 7 km). So, in the first case we filter out provider 5164, in the second we don't filter it out. However, the user location is very close for both delivery address, no way it is ~3 km distance between those two. Could it be something on how you compute the distance on {{"/internal/getRouteDistanceFromProvidersToEater"}}  ?PS: Another explanation might be that even though the delivery point are very close one another, the distance might be computed so different due to some routes that the courier needs to take to get to one point vs the other ? This is just a wild guess from myself

If no user is logged, then the call to pricing is not happening and we are using air distance as per here:


{noformat}public async getProvidersDistances(
    ctx: Context,
    providers: ProviderModel[],
    maxDeliveryDistance: number,
    isRouteDistanceEnabled: boolean,
    userLocation: LatLng,
    userId: number | null,
    appVersion: string
): Promise<DistanceInformation> {
    const distanceInfo: DistanceInformation = {
        provider_distance_to_eater: {},
        city_discovery_distance_km: maxDeliveryDistance,
        is_route_distance_enabled_for_user: isRouteDistanceEnabled && !!userId
    };

    if (distanceInfo.is_route_distance_enabled_for_user) {
        distanceInfo.provider_distance_to_eater = await this.deliveryPricingApiService.getRouteDistances(
            ctx,
            appVersion,
            userId!,
            userLocation,
            providers
        );
    }

    for (const provider of providers) {
        await EventLoopDeferrer.defer();
        if (!!distanceInfo.provider_distance_to_eater[provider.id]?.distance_in_km) {
            distanceInfo.provider_distance_to_eater[provider.id].is_route_distance = true;
            continue;
        }

        distanceInfo.provider_distance_to_eater[provider.id] = {
            distance_in_km: DistanceOnEarth.getDistance(
                userLocation.lat,
                userLocation.lng,
                provider.location.lat,
                provider.location.lng
            )
        };
    }{noformat}

Privacy Assessment of why we can share this info:

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
According to para 107 of EDPB Guidelines 01/2022 on data subject rights - Right of access:
{panel}

“In case of identity theft, a person fraudulently acts in the name of another person. In this context it is important to recall that the victim should be provided with information on all personal data the controller stores in connection with their identity, including those that have been collected on the basis of the fraudster’s actions. *_In other words, even after the controller learned about the identity theft, personal data which are associated with or related to the identity of the victim constitute personal data of the data subject_*.”



It means that Bolt is entitled to share this data with the user as this data is necessary for the user to secure/block their card and investigate the case. This is for the benefit of the user. Bolt legitimate interest is the customer trust and facilitation of the fraud investigation. Moreover, it reduces the amount of police requests submitted to Bolt.

